{
  "description": "One number formatter for every value on the display (issue eink-ha-os#85; emulator src/core/format.ts fmtValue/kw, firmware core/logic.cpp fmtValue/kw). 1. HA display_precision (entity registry options.sensor.display_precision or suggested_display_precision, or a display_precision state attribute) wins: exactly that many decimals. 2. Otherwise per unit: W 0, kW 2, kWh 1, % 0, °C 1, °F 1, V 1, A 1 (fixed decimals); any other unit, or none, keeps up to 2 decimals with trailing zeros trimmed. 3. A state that is not a plain decimal number (optional sign, digits, optional fraction, optional exponent) passes through unchanged. Ties round like Number.prototype.toFixed; a result that is zero never shows a minus sign. kw: |watts| >= 1000 shows kW (per-unit default, display_precision does not apply after the conversion), else W (display_precision applies). Number format (eink-ha-os#110): \"cases\" and \"kw\" use the point format. The result is then written in the display's number format: from HA's user profile number_format (frontend/get_user_data key \"language\") when it is comma_decimal (1,250.5), decimal_comma (1.250,5) or space_comma (1 250,5), with a group separator every 3 integer digits; \"none\" is the point format; \"language\", \"system\" or unset follow the language: Dutch a decimal comma (2,1), anything else a point, never a group separator (1250). fewerDecimals (eink-ha-os#151): a shown number in its number format with one decimal less, rounded like toFixed; no decimals or not a number unchanged. A tile whose value and unit do not fit drops decimals before the unit is cut. fitValue (eink-ha-os#162): the value and size for a tile; sizes descending, width(value, size) = floor(codepoints(value) x size / 10) + unit. Pass 1: for each size, decimals drop (fewerDecimals) while the result keeps 3 significant digits (digits from the first non-zero one); pass 2: the same with 2; the first size where width <= maxW wins. If none fits: the smallest size, decimals dropped until it fits or none are left. Never an ellipsis. fitMiddle (eink-ha-os#215): a label (the OTA version) for maxW; same width function without a unit; the first size where it fits whole wins, else the smallest size with the middle replaced by \"…\": for the largest k (codepoints kept) that fits, the first ceil(k/2) and the last floor(k/2) codepoints; nothing fits → \"…\".",
